<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmed al-Fateh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1796">1796</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Ahmad ibn Muhammad Al Khalifa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmed al-Fateh, Ahmad ibn Muhammad Al <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalifa">Khalifa</a>, was the first Al Khalifa ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain">Bahrain</a>. In 1783 the Al Khalifa and their allies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bani-utbah">Bani Utbah</a>, based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zubarah">Zubarah</a> in Qatar, crossed to Bahrain and drove out the governor serving the sheikhs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bushehr">Bushehr</a>, earning him the name al-Fateh, &quot;the Conqueror&quot;. He ruled until his death in 1796, and his descendants still rule Bahrain.</p></div>
